IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `gst-types`

-- Goods and Services Tax Act 1993 — GOAL 3: WHAT INPUT TAX MAY BE CLAIMED,
-- AND WHAT IS THE NET AMOUNT DUE?
--
--   "May this input tax be credited, and how much of it; must it be repaid if
--    the supplier is not paid; what is the net tax or refund for the period;
--    and what surcharge follows a claim on a fraudulent chain?"
--
-- Source: ../source/GSTA1993.txt — Part 4 (ss 19-20), ss 41(7)-(8), 45A, the
-- Ninth Schedule.

§ `Goal 3 — input tax and the net amount`

-- s 20(2D): a person "should have known" a supply was part of an arrangement
-- causing loss of revenue if "(a) the circumstances ... carried a reasonable
-- risk ...; and (b) the taxable person, before making a claim ... (i) did not
-- take reasonable steps ...; or (ii) took reasonable steps and ... concluded
-- [unreasonably], was unable to conclude, or did not conclude". s 20(2F): not
-- if it took reasonable steps and reached a conclusion a reasonable person
-- would have made.
@ref s 20(2D)-(2F)
GIVEN i IS AN `Input tax facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person should have known of the arrangement` i IF
    i's `circumstances carried a reasonable risk` AND (NOT i's `took reasonable steps and reasonably concluded it was not`)

-- s 19(3)(a): input tax is tax on goods or services "used or to be used for
-- the purpose of any business"; s 19(4): partly business use is apportioned
-- "so that only so much as is referable to the taxable person's business
-- purposes is counted". s 20(1)-(2): credit only for input tax attributable to
-- taxable and the other listed supplies. s 20(2A): none on a supply "which the
-- taxable person knew or should have known was a part of any arrangement to
-- cause loss of public revenue".
@ref ss 19(3)-(4), 20(1)-(2A)
GIVEN i IS AN `Input tax facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the input tax may be credited` i IF
        i's `for the purpose of the business`
    AND i's `attributable to supplies within s 20(2)`
    AND NOT (i's `part of an arrangement causing loss of revenue` AND (i's `knew it` OR `the person should have known of the arrangement` i))

@ref s 19(4)
GIVEN i IS AN `Input tax facts`, tax IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the creditable input tax, facts` i `, tax charged` tax MEANS
    IF `the input tax may be credited` i
    THEN tax TIMES i's `share used for business purposes, per cent` DIVIDED BY 100
    ELSE 0

-- s 41(7): at the end of a period the net tax due, or the amount due to the
-- person under s 19(5), "is zero if the amount is less than $5". s 19(5): if
-- credit exceeds output tax, the excess is paid to the person.
@ref ss 19(2), (5), 41(7)
GIVEN output IS A NUMBER, input IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the net tax due, output` output `, input` input MEANS
    IF `the difference` LESS THAN 5 AND `the difference` GREATER THAN (0 MINUS 5)
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the difference`
    WHERE
        `the difference` MEANS output MINUS input

-- s 19(12): input tax credited on a supply the person has not paid for must
-- be repaid "in the prescribed accounting period during which the initial
-- specified period expires" — "12 months after the due date for payment".
-- (12A), (15): if paid later in the "subsequent specified period" (ending
-- "5 years after the end of" the period of the first claim, or 6 years before
-- 2007), it may be claimed again.
@ref s 19(12), (15) "initial specified period"
GIVEN `payment due` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`unpaid input tax must be repaid in the period containing, payment due` `payment due` MEANS `add months` `payment due` 12

@ref s 19(12A), (15) "subsequent specified period"
GIVEN `period of first claim ended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`repaid input tax may be reclaimed until, first claim period ended` `period of first claim ended` MEANS
    IF `period of first claim ended` LESS THAN YMD 2007 1 1
    THEN `add years` `period of first claim ended` 6
    ELSE `add years` `period of first claim ended` 5

-- s 45A(1): a claim on a supply the person "should have known was a part of an
-- arrangement" attracts "a surcharge equal to 10% of the amount of the input
-- tax"; (3) payable "within one month after" notice.
@ref s 45A(1)
GIVEN `input tax claimed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the surcharge on a tainted claim of` `input tax claimed` MEANS `input tax claimed` TIMES 10 DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 34A(1)-(2): on a transfer of a going concern between taxable persons
-- outside the scope by order, the transferee is deemed to have incurred and
-- deducted input tax on the asset value "without the addition of tax".
@ref s 34A(1)-(2)
GIVEN `asset value` IS A NUMBER, rate IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deemed input tax on a going concern's assets, value` `asset value` `, rate` rate MEANS
    `asset value` TIMES rate DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `Provisions carried as text`

@ref ss 19(1), (3A), (5A)-(11), (13)-(14A), 20(2B)-(2C), (2G), (3)-(5); Ninth Schedule
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`credit provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "s 19(1), (6)-(11), (13)-(14A): accounting periods, hold-over, withholding refunds from non-filers, claims within the prescribed time, interest on late refunds, documentary evidence, pre-registration and pre-incorporation tax, blocked input tax, bare trustees"
         "s 19(3A), (5A): import GST deferred under s 27A counts only once accounted for, and reduces the refund"
         "s 20(2B)-(2C), (2G): what an arrangement causing loss of public revenue is, and the risk circumstances (the Ninth Schedule's five illustrations)"
         "s 20(3)-(5): regulations on de minimis exempt supplies and attribution"
